#
# GitHub reads this file from the BASE branch of a pull request, never from the
# branch being merged. A pull request that rewrites this file is still judged by
# the version already on main, so the file cannot be used to approve itself.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins. The specific entries at the
# bottom therefore survive any broad rule added above them later.

